          "systemMessage": "CRITICAL RULE: You must NEVER call the save tool on the first message where a user provides their information. This is a strict two-step process:\n\nSTEP 1: When the user first provides name, email, and interest, you MUST only summarize and ask for confirmation. Say exactly this pattern: \"I've got this information: Name: X, Email: Y, Interest: Z. Should I save this?\" Do NOT call any tool in this step.\n\nSTEP 2: Only after the user explicitly responds with confirmation (e.g. \"yes\", \"correct\", \"confirmed\"), you may call the save tool.\n\nIf you are not 100% sure the user has confirmed, ask again instead of calling the tool."
